# Allowed commit scopes, one per line. Blank lines and `#` comment lines are
# ignored. A trailing comment on a scope line is not: `tools/check-scoped-commit.ts`
# compares the whole trimmed line, so `theme  # ...` would stop matching `theme`.
#
# This file is the only list. The check has no built-in scopes; it also accepts
# the name of a real proposal file — `proposals/<NNNN>-<slug>.md` is the scope
# `<NNNN>-<slug>` — so feature work needs no entry here.
#
# Prefer the narrowest scope that accurately describes the change. Add a scope
# in the same commit that first needs it.

